  "text": {
    "intro": "The Inverlaig ferry runs a full day of crossings in theory, and a variable number in practice.\nFive skippers are involved. Determine each skipper's start time, cargo, vessel and reason.\n- **Skipper**: Ruaridh, Senga, Tormod, Fearghas and Eilidh.\n- **Start time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Notable cargo**: a wedding party; a brass band; nineteen sheep; a film crew and no permits; and a church organ.\n- **Vessel**: the Steadfast, the Siller Grey, the Three Brothers, the Kelpie and the Ailsa Belle.\n- **Delay blamed on**: fog, paperwork, the tide, a slipway repair and a missing deckhand.\nEvery skipper has a different start time, cargo, vessel and reason, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The skipper who commands the Ailsa Belle sails at 8am. The skipper who blames a slipway repair and 8am are exactly four hours apart in start time order.",
      "The skipper who carries a church organ commands the Three Brothers.",
      "Senga does not sail at noon.",
      "The skipper who commands the Steadfast is exactly one hour earlier than the skipper who carries a brass band, with no start time in between.",
      "The skipper who carries a wedding party is exactly one hour earlier than Tormod, with no start time in between.",
      "The skipper who carries a brass band and the skipper who blames the tide are exactly four hours apart in start time order.",
      "Eilidh is exactly one hour earlier than the skipper who blames a missing deckhand, with no start time in between.",
      "The skipper who carries nineteen sheep and the skipper who blames the tide are exactly three hours apart in start time order.",
      "The skipper who blames fog is exactly one hour earlier than the skipper who carries a church organ, with no start time in between.",
      "Senga does not blame a missing deckhand. The skipper who commands the Kelpie falls somewhere between the skipper who blames a missing deckhand and Ruaridh in start time order."
    ]
  }
